.TH smi-extract "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-extract, smi-xvzf, smi-xvjf, smi-xvJf \- Extract a tar archive into a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-xvzf
.I TAR_FILE DESTINATION_DIR
.RB [ ALL_IN_ROOT= true ]
.RB [ VERBOSE= false ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-extract
extracts
.I TAR_FILE
into
.IR DESTINATION_DIR ,
creating the directory when it does not exist.
By default the first path component of the archive is dropped, so an archive whose files sit
under one top directory unpacks its contents directly into
.IR DESTINATION_DIR .
.PP
The tar flags come from the name the command is started under: the part after the last
.B -
is appended to
.BR tar\ -x .
It is therefore used through its links, not by the name
.BR smi-extract :
.TP
.B smi-xvzf
gzip,
.B .tar.gz
and
.BR .tgz .
.TP
.B smi-xvjf
bzip2,
.BR .tar.bz2 .
.TP
.B smi-xvJf
xz,
.BR .tar.xz .
.PP
The links are created in
.I /opt/setmy.info/bin
by the rpm and deb install scripts and removed again on uninstall.
A link named
.BI smi-x[v] {z|j|J} f
works the same way, so
.B smi-xzf
is gzip as well.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I TAR_FILE
Archive to extract.
.TP
.I DESTINATION_DIR
Directory to extract into, created with
.B mkdir -p
when missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
Options are given after the two arguments, as
.IR KEY = VALUE ,
in any order. They are shell assignments, evaluated as written.
.TP
.B ALL_IN_ROOT=true
Keeps the archive layout as it is,
.BR --strip-components=0 ,
for an archive whose files are already in its root.
The default,
.BR false ,
drops the first path component,
.BR --strip-components=1 .
.TP
.B VERBOSE=false
Leaves out the
.B v
this option adds.
The extracted files are listed by default.
The links named
.BI smi-xv ... f
carry a
.B v
in the name as well, and that one is always part of the flags, so a quiet extraction needs both a
link without it and the option:
.B smi-xzf
.I TAR_FILE DESTINATION_DIR
.BR VERBOSE=false .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
The exit status of
.BR tar (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Unpack a release whose files are under one top directory:
.RS
.nf
smi-xvzf app-1.0.0.tar.gz /var/opt/a/deploy
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unpack an archive that has its files in the root:
.RS
.nf
smi-xvJf site.tar.xz /usr/share/nginx/html ALL_IN_ROOT=true
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
.PP
Report smi-extract bugs to \fIinfo@setmy.info\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
